## Change

- Java `ServiceThread` declares `shutdown()` and `shutdown(boolean)`; the
  no-argument method dispatches to the boolean form with `false`.
- Rust now exposes `RuntimeServiceThread::shutdown()` and
  `shutdown_with_interrupt(bool)` for those overloads. PullMessageService
  retains its dynamic override behavior and closes the scheduled executor on
  pre-start shutdown.
- The Java fixture invokes no-argument shutdown on unstarted worker instances;
  Rust tests cover pre-start stopped flags, pre-start scheduler closure, normal
  shutdown, and the explicit interrupt path.
- The unchanged `fixtures/runtime/client-config.json` SHA-256 is
  `aff5aa095941819f7cb3a1f419a66000e5b83177f7badd0d4625b85552e53387`.

